; EmuV0 1.12 as its archive installs it, but in RAM only: the system's
; SYS:Tools/EmuV0 copied, the 1.12 archive laid over it, and the two assigns
; pointed at the copy. Nothing on the disk changes; a reboot undoes it.
Copy SYS:Tools/EmuV0 RAM:emu112 ALL QUIET
Copy RAM:rxt/emu112/EmuV0/Tools/EmuV0 RAM:emu112 ALL QUIET
Copy RAM:rxt/emu112/EmuV0/C/EmuV0-pc RAM:emu112/EmuV0-pc
Protect RAM:emu112/EmuV0-pc +e
Assign EmuV0: RAM:emu112
Assign LIBSV0: EmuV0:Libs
Assign LIBSV0: EmuV0:Classes ADD
